WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
John Wick is Keanu Reeves' most physical&nbsp;
role, and the actor has to be pretty ripped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:08.680
to play the famed assassin. According to&nbsp;
Men's Health, Reeves used a surprisingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.300
limited workout routine to prepare for&nbsp;
the role, with just six central movements.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:17.800
First, Reeves performs a reverse lunge front&nbsp;
dumbbell raise, which impacts the legs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.780
shoulders, and chest. Next up, there's the BOSU&nbsp;
lunge shoulder press. This works out the lower&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.940
body and shoulders, as well as developing balance.&nbsp;
Then there's the reverse-step resistance band row,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.300
which continues the lower body&nbsp;
workout while also working the back.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.920
There's also the squat with TRX shoulder&nbsp;
iso-hold, which hits the lower body and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.340
shoulders. Reeves follows that with&nbsp;
the stability ball dynamic plank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:44.080
which develops core strength and balance. He&nbsp;
finishes with the banded lateral walk pallof&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.220
press, which helps to develop shoulder width&nbsp;
and leaves mere mortals feeling pretty sore.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.700
The full routine ensures that a&nbsp;
person is both strong and mobile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.220
which comes in handy for martial arts training.

